# Planted bugs for the SCD2 model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy scd2.als
properties NoOverlap_MergeClosesPriorRowAtomically OneCurrentRow_MergeClosesPriorRowAtomically
file scd2.als

mutation two prior rows can both close into the same next row
detects NoOverlap_MergeClosesPriorRowAtomically
-   all r, r2: Row | (r.key = r2.key and r != r2 and not Current[r] and not Current[r2]) implies r.validTo != r2.validTo
+   all r, r2: Row | (r.key = r2.key and r != r2 and not Current[r] and not Current[r2]) implies r.validTo = r.validTo

mutation a key can have more than one current row at once
detects OneCurrentRow_MergeClosesPriorRowAtomically
-   all k: Key | lone r: Row | r.key = k and Current[r]
+   all k: Key | some r: Row | r.key = k and Current[r]

harmless a comment on Covers is reworded
- -- A row is the active one for its key at instant i.
+ -- Whether this row is the one in force for its key at instant i.
